      <div class="prose">
        <p>The bug I keep finding is the same one wearing different clothes: a system reports a state it is not in. A policy engine says <b>pass</b> after checking zero resources. A gateway marks a policy <b>Accepted</b> while Envoy rejects the backend. A rollback says <b>Synced</b> while the old revision runs.</p>
        <p>Nobody files these, because nothing looks broken. The dashboard is green. So I read the status, then go and look at what actually happened -- the goroutine count, the Envoy config, the task set tag -- and write down the difference.</p>
        <p>Every fix I send comes with the measurement that shows the gap. A claim I can't reproduce doesn't get posted.</p>
        <p class="dim">Merged in Kyverno, KEDA and PipeCD, with fixes in review at Volcano, Kubeflow, kgateway, OpenKruise and KubeEdge. Looking for internships.</p>
